  "name": "Pharmaceutical Batch Plant",
  "category": "mixed",
  "description": "GxP oral-solid-dose plant: corporate LAN with LIMS and QA, an IT/OT DMZ (historian replica, jump host) and plant operations with a FactoryTalk Batch server, PI historian, Werum-style MES, engineering station, DeltaV ProfessionalPLUS + Application Station, operator HMIs, a recipe/report file share and a GxP audit-trail syslog collector. GRANULATION (PlantPAx): ControlLogix 5580 unit controllers phase-managed by the batch server over CIP, with POINT I/O adapters and PowerFlex 755 drives on class-1 I/O. FORMULATION: Emerson DeltaV PK controllers served over OPC UA to the Application Station. Every GxP server and the engineering station forward audit events to AUDIT01 by syslog. Recipe parameters reach the unit controllers as Logix Write Tag downloads (enip-write) from the batch server and the engineering station. Planted findings (see findings[]): a recipe change from a non-engineering corporate host, a shared service account on the recipe share, a corporate host reaching plant operations without the DMZ. Periods: CIP phase polling 1 s, class-1 I/O 100 ms (Forward_Open states a 20 ms RPI), OPC UA 1-5 s, recipe downloads every 4-8 h, audit syslog 60 s.",
